# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the two values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings > API). Then restart the bundler: npx expo start --clear
#
# Both are safe to ship in the app bundle — the publishable/anon key grants
# nothing on its own. Row Level Security is what protects the data, and it is
# enforced by Postgres regardless of who is holding this key.
#
# The SERVICE ROLE key is a different thing entirely. It bypasses RLS. It must
# never appear in this file, in the app, or in git. It lives only in the Supabase
# dashboard, where the Edge Functions read it from their environment.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-or-anon-key

# Push notifications need an EAS project id. Without one, the Expo push service
# will not issue a token and every alert lands in the in-app inbox only — which
# for "your van is due in 15 minutes" is the same as not sending it.
#
# Get one with `npx eas init`. This overrides extra.eas.projectId in app.json.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_EAS_PROJECT_ID=
